## What was wrong

The code half had already landed and was verified live — this session's own context opens with [PROJECT-INSTRUCTIONS-<nonce>-BEGIN CLAUDE.md]. But CLAUDE.md was never touched despite being in the task's Files: line, and worse, it asserted the opposite of what shipped:

│ "Every byte of a hostile CLAUDE.md still reaches the model exactly as before, load_project_context's return value is unchanged"

That return value is exactly what the change modified — a false authoritative claim in the one file re-injected as context every session.

## What I did

Measured before writing, rather than transcribing from the diff. I read the actual shipped functions and doc comments, then ran the positive control myself instead of documenting numbers I hadn't seen:

• Neutered wrap_project_instruction to return content unchanged (marked NEUTERED, one atomic mutate→run→restore) → exactly 3 red, 31 passed, byte-empty restore, 0 markers.
• Read the surviving green and found both survivors are weaker than they look: the "never tells the model to discount" test asserts absence of banned words, which a dead branch satisfies identically (boundary pin, not a guard); and the byte-identity guard drives a fixture with no instruction file, so the neutered function is never called — it was structurally incapable of failing under that control.

Two things I deliberately stated against my own interest, because the flattering version was available:

1. One of the 3 red tests is the pre-existing separator test inverted in the same diff, not a new one. So the mechanism wasn't virgin territory — it had a guard pinning the opposite convention. The claim shrinks accordingly (Day-190 rule).
2. The real finding the diff exposed: the old --- From <path> --- separator was applied only to secondary files, so the first instruction file — in this repo, CLAUDE.md itself — arrived with no provenance marker at all. The highest-influence file in the prompt was the one guaranteed to be unlabelled.

Scope held. src/context.rs is 1387 lines, un-listed and far under the 2000 cap, so no register line was owed — I checked with cargo fmt run before reading the number. The one size warning the gate prints is src/cli.rs drift (+25) that predates this diff and sits in neither the Files: line nor the task scope, so I left it and said so rather than quietly widening a verified narrow change.

